# GeoQoE Pulse — local context retrieval
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory and fill in one API key.
# `.env` is gitignored; this example file is not. Never commit a real key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# A real shell environment variable always overrides the value set here, so
# existing `export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...` workflows keep working unchanged.
#
# With no key set, the dashboard still runs: cached briefs in data/context/ are
# served normally and uncached cells return "no corroborated upcoming context
# found" — the same output a genuinely empty search produces.


# ===========================================================================
# TWO WAYS TO RUN THIS
#
# A) Separate search  (free)   SEARCH_PROVIDER + CONTEXT_PROVIDER
#      A dedicated search API retrieves the sources; the language model only
#      reads them. Both halves have real free tiers, and this file caps the
#      snippet length, so the request cannot outgrow a free-tier token limit.
#      THIS IS THE ONLY GENUINELY FREE CONFIGURATION.
#
# B) Provider-native search    CONTEXT_PROVIDER alone
#      One API both searches and reasons. Simpler, but every free tier
#      withholds the search half - see the Groq and Gemini notes below.
# ===========================================================================

# --- A) Separate search provider (leave blank to use provider-native search)
# One of: exa, serper, tavily
#
#   exa     $20 on signup + $10/month, ~20k requests/month, no card
#   serper  2,500 searches/month
#   tavily  1,000 searches/month
#
# Each brief runs 3 queries, so 2,500/month is ~830 briefs.
SEARCH_PROVIDER=exa
EXA_API_KEY=
SERPER_API_KEY=
TAVILY_API_KEY=


# --- B) The language model (always required - it reasons either way)
# One of: perplexity, anthropic, groq, gemini, openrouter
#
# With SEARCH_PROVIDER set, the model is NOT asked to search and a plain model
# is selected automatically (Groq uses llama-3.3-70b-versatile, not compound).
#
# Only providers that run web search server-side AND report which pages they
# retrieved are supported. That report is what the grounding check verifies
# every event against. A provider without it would return confident, invented
# events, so there is deliberately no generic "any OpenAI-compatible endpoint".
CONTEXT_PROVIDER=gemini

# --- Perplexity ------------------------------------------------------------
# Default model: sonar (sonar-pro for stronger reasoning, ~3x the token cost)
# Key from https://www.perplexity.ai/account/api
#
# NOT free: pay-as-you-go, roughly $5-14 per 1,000 requests for search plus
# ~$1/M tokens on sonar. Pre-warming 10 demo cells costs single-digit cents.
# New API accounts have historically carried trial credits - check on signup.
#
# Best technical fit of the search-capable providers: Sonar compresses its
# search results before they reach the model, which is exactly what Groq's
# compound systems fail to do (see the 413 note below).
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# --- Anthropic -------------------------------------------------------------
# Default model: claude-opus-5 (server-side web_search tool)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Google AI Studio ------------------------------------------------------
# Default model: gemini-3.5-flash (Grounding with Google Search)
# Key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — has a free tier.
#
# NOTE: Google's grounding terms require displaying the Search Suggestions that
# come back in groundingMetadata.searchEntryPoint. The dashboard does not render
# them today. Check this before publishing the dashboard outside a demo.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter ------------------------------------------------------------
# Default model: google/gemini-3.5-flash, with the `web` search plugin, which
# adds search to any model it routes to. Search is billed per result on top of
# the model's own tokens.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Groq ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default model: groq/compound
#
# KNOWN BROKEN on low-tier Groq accounts (tested 2026-09-21): any compound
# request that triggers a web search returns HTTP 413 Request Entity Too Large,
# because the search results exceed the account's per-request token cap before
# the reply is returned. It fails identically for a one-line prompt, and neither
# lowering max_completion_tokens nor restricting search domains avoids it.
# Raise the account's limits, or use another provider.
#
# Only Groq's *compound* systems run web search at all. A plain chat model
# (llama-3.3-70b-versatile and similar) has none, so every "event" it returned
# would be invented, all of them discarded, and the panel always empty.
# Do not point CONTEXT_MODEL at a non-compound Groq model.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Optional overrides ----------------------------------------------------
# Override the provider's default model.
# CONTEXT_MODEL=

# Request timeout in milliseconds. Web search plus reasoning routinely takes
# 30-60 seconds, so do not lower this much below the default.
# CONTEXT_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
